  "description": "TEMVOZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C101 H112 Cr1 Ho6 N1 O40,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.445-3.769 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.61-106.30°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CrHo6(OH)8(o-tol)12(NO3)(MeOH)5]·2MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ho(III).",
